@startbpmn BP15_ReviewArchivedMaterial
lang en

output L1 "01_detailed/BP15_ReviewArchivedMaterial.bpmn"
output L2 "02_detailed/BP15_ReviewArchivedMaterial.bpmn"

' Provenance (never in a drawn note, lint rule 5):
'   - archived items are retained, hidden from the working view, read by an explicit act: BR-26
'   - an archived item cannot be edited, any archived item: BR-05, SA 2026-10-10
'   - unarchive must leave the overall state consistent and is rejected whenever it cannot: BR-25
'   - a partial unarchive can never be consistent and is refused in either direction: BR-25
'   - the bundle comes back in its prior state and prior position: BR-25
'   - an archived item's position is never occupied while it is away: BR-25
'   - where the bundle cannot be reassembled the item stays archived: BR-25
'   - four archivable kinds: idea, goal, project with its activities and tasks, task: BR-23
'   - an archived goal carries its check-out record, and unarchiving never revokes it: BR-30
'   - a goal's measures and their check-in history come back with it: BR-112
'   - the archive view's filters and default sorts belong to the Contract gate: BR-26
'
' Scope: this process reads the archive and brings things back. Putting them there is each entity's
' own process, and the archive is no shield from a deletion, so an item can also leave the archive
' by being deleted out of it, which is BP02, BP04, BP05, BP11, BP17 or BP18 rather than this one.
'
' Call-site collapsing: the four archivable kinds are not four operations. Reading the archived
' ideas, goals, projects and tasks is one request with the kind and the filter as its payload, and
' unarchiving is one request whose consequences differ by what the item carries rather than by
' which operation is called. This is why the eight candidates in Intent section 6 draw as three.

pool "User" {
  start "Something to look up, or something to bring back"
  task "Open the archive" as archive
  send "Read the archived items" to listIn
  receive "The archived items of that kind" as list

  if "What needs doing?" then "narrow or re-scope the list"
    :Change the kind or the filter in force;
    note "The archive is read by an explicit act. Nothing archived shows up in the working view."
    goto archive

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "read one"
    :Read the item as it stands;
    note "An archived item is readable and frozen. Changing one means bringing it back first, and an archived goal still carries its check-out record."

  else "bring one back"
    :Choose an item to unarchive;
    send "See what unarchiving will bring back" to impactIn
    receive "What comes back, or why it cannot" as impact
    if "Can the bundle come back whole?" rule BR-25 then "yes"
      :Confirm the unarchiving;
      send "Unarchive an item" to unarchiveIn
      receive "The item back in the working set" as unarchived
      note "The whole bundle comes back as it went. No part of it can be picked and nothing is re-parented, relocated or approximated."
    else "no"
      :Read why it stays archived;
      note "A member deleted out of the archive, or a surrounding that is now gone, leaves the bundle unreassemblable. The item stays archived."
    endif
  endif

  if "Anything else in the archive?" then "yes"
    goto archive
  else "no"
    :Leave the archive;
  endif

  end "Archive reviewed"
}

system pool "Bearing" {
  messageStart "Archive list requested" as listIn
  call "BP15.01_ReadTheArchivedItems" "Read the archived items" {
    :Read the archived items of the kind asked for;
    rule BR-26
    :Apply the filter and the sort in force;
    rule BR-88
    :Carry each archived goal's check-out record with it;
    rule BR-30
  }
  send "The archived items of that kind" to list
  note "One request serves all four archivable kinds: ideas, goals, projects and tasks. Archived material is retained on disk and reachable only this way."
  end "Archive list answered"

  messageStart "Unarchive impact requested" as impactIn
  call "BP15.02_ReadTheUnarchiveImpact" "See what unarchiving will bring back" {
    :Collect the whole bundle the item was archived with;
    rule BR-25
    :Check that every member is still there;
    :Check that the surroundings can still hold it;
    :Report what comes back, or what is missing;
    rule BR-25
  }
  send "What comes back, or why it cannot" to impact
  note "A project brings its activities and their tasks; a goal brings its measures and their check-in history. The bundle is judged whole: a subset is never offered."
  end "Unarchive impact answered"

  messageStart "Unarchive requested" as unarchiveIn
  call "BP15.03_UnarchiveItem" "Unarchive an item" {
    if "Is the bundle reassemblable?" rule BR-25 then "yes"
      :Return every member to its prior state;
      :Return every member to its prior position;
      rule BR-88
    else "no"
      :Refuse the unarchiving and say what is missing;
    endif
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The item back in the working set" to unarchived
  note "Ordering is relative, so the position an archived item comes back to was never occupied while it was away. The check-out record of a goal that comes back is untouched."
  end "Unarchive answered"
}

@endbpmn
